# Next.js Development Guide (LLM Rulebook)

## Purpose

Project structure, TypeScript configuration, naming conventions, and package management for Next.js applications. Apply when setting up or modifying Next.js projects. DO NOT apply to backend-only services.

## Project Structure (MUST)

### Top-level Organization

```
project-root/
├── src/
│   ├── app/           # Next.js App Router
│   ├── components/    # React components
│   ├── lib/           # Utilities and shared code
│   └── styles/        # Global styles
├── test/              # All test files
├── public/            # Static assets
├── package.json
└── tsconfig.json
```

### Source Directory

```
src/
├── app/
│   ├── layout.tsx     # Root layout
│   ├── page.tsx       # Homepage
│   └── [feature]/     # Feature routes
│       ├── page.tsx
│       └── layout.tsx
├── components/
│   ├── ui/            # Base components
│   └── features/      # Feature-specific components
├── lib/
│   ├── utils.ts       # General utilities
│   ├── types.ts       # Shared type definitions
│   └── constants.ts   # Application constants
└── styles/
    └── globals.css
```

### Test Directory

```
test/
├── unit/
│   ├── components/
│   │   └── ui/
│   │       └── Button.test.tsx
│   └── lib/
│       └── utils.test.ts
└── integration/
    └── auth-flow.test.tsx
```

## Naming Conventions (MUST)

### Files and Directories

- Directories: kebab-case (`user-profile/`)
- Utility files: kebab-case (`form-utils.ts`)
- Component files: PascalCase (`Button.tsx`)
- Test files: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

### Components

```
components/
├── ui/
│   ├── Button.tsx
│   ├── Card.tsx
│   └── TextField.tsx
└── features/
    ├── auth/
    │   ├── LoginForm.tsx
    │   └── SignupForm.tsx
    └── dashboard/
        └── ActivityChart.tsx
```

## TypeScript Configuration (MUST)

### tsconfig.json

```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "es2017",
    "lib": ["dom", "dom.iterable", "esnext"],
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "jsx": "preserve",
    "incremental": true,
    "plugins": [{ "name": "next" }],
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["next-env.d.ts", "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", ".next/types/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
```

### Strict Options

```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noImplicitAny": true,
    "strictNullChecks": true,
    "strictFunctionTypes": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true
  }
}
```

## Import Conventions (MUST)

### Aliases

```typescript
// tsconfig.json paths
{
  "@/*": ["./src/*"]
}

// Usage
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/Button"
import { useAuth } from "@/lib/auth"
```

### Import Order

```typescript
// 1. External dependencies (alphabetical)
import { useState } from "react"
import { z } from "zod"

// 2. Internal modules (by path depth, then alphabetical)
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/Button"
import { useAuth } from "@/lib/auth"

// 3. Types and styles last
import type { User } from "@/lib/types"
import "@/styles/module.css"
```

### Barrel Exports

```typescript
// src/components/ui/index.ts
export { Button } from "./Button"
export { Card } from "./Card"
export { TextField } from "./TextField"

// Usage
import { Button, Card, TextField } from "@/components/ui"
```

## Component Structure (MUST)

### File Organization

```typescript
// src/components/features/auth/LoginForm.tsx

// 1. Imports
import { useState } from "react"
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/Button"

// 2. Types
interface LoginFormProps {
  onSuccess?: () => void
}

// 3. Component definition
export function LoginForm({ onSuccess }: LoginFormProps) {
  return (
    <form>
      {/* Component JSX */}
    </form>
  )
}
```

### Client Component Annotation

```typescript
"use client"

import { useState } from "react"
// Rest of component
```

### Prop Typing

```typescript
// Direct interface
interface ButtonProps {
  variant?: "primary" | "secondary" | "outline"
  size?: "sm" | "md" | "lg"
  isLoading?: boolean
  children: React.ReactNode
}

// Extending HTML element
import { ComponentPropsWithoutRef } from "react"

interface ButtonProps extends ComponentPropsWithoutRef<"button"> {
  variant?: "primary" | "secondary" | "outline"
  isLoading?: boolean
}
```

## Route Organization (MUST)

### App Router Structure

```
src/app/
├── layout.tsx         # Root layout
├── page.tsx           # Homepage
├── auth/
│   ├── login/
│   │   └── page.tsx
│   └── signup/
│       └── page.tsx
└── dashboard/
    ├── layout.tsx     # Dashboard layout
    ├── page.tsx       # Dashboard index
    └── settings/
        └── page.tsx
```

### Route Grouping

```
src/app/
├── (marketing)/       # Marketing pages group
│   ├── layout.tsx
│   ├── page.tsx
│   └── about/
│       └── page.tsx
└── (app)/             # Authenticated app group
    ├── layout.tsx
    └── dashboard/
        └── page.tsx
```

## Package Management (MUST)

Use `pnpm` exclusively:

```bash
# Install dependencies
pnpm install

# Add dependency
pnpm add react-query

# Add dev dependency
pnpm add -D typescript

# Run scripts
pnpm dev
pnpm build
pnpm test
```

### package.json Scripts

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "next dev",
    "build": "next build",
    "start": "next start",
    "lint": "next lint",
    "test": "jest",
    "test:watch": "jest --watch"
  }
}
```

## Type Declarations (MUST)

### Organization

```
src/lib/types/
├── api/           # API related types
├── models/        # Domain models
├── components/    # Component props
└── index.ts       # Re-exports
```

### Common Types

```typescript
// lib/types/api.ts
export interface ApiResponse<T> {
  data: T
  meta?: {
    page?: number
    limit?: number
    total?: number
  }
}

export interface ApiError {
  code: string
  message: string
  details?: Record<string, unknown>
}

// lib/types/models.ts
export interface User {
  id: string
  name: string
  email: string
  createdAt: string
}
```

### Type Guards

```typescript
// lib/utils/type-guards.ts
import { User } from "@/lib/types"

export function isUser(obj: unknown): obj is User {
  return (
    obj !== null &&
    typeof obj === "object" &&
    "id" in obj &&
    "name" in obj &&
    "email" in obj
  )
}
```

## Environment Variables (MUST)

### Type-safe Environment

```typescript
// types/env.d.ts
declare namespace NodeJS {
  interface ProcessEnv {
    NODE_ENV: "development" | "production" | "test"
    NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL: string
    DATABASE_URL: string
  }
}
```

### File Organization

```
project-root/
├── .env                # Default (committed)
├── .env.local          # Local overrides (not committed)
├── .env.development    # Development (committed)
└── .env.production     # Production (committed)
```

